ORFik 1.29.16
=============

Transcript mapping and accessors
-------------------------------

    o Bug fix: empty transcript ranges (end = start - 1) map again to empty genomic
      ranges, as before the C++ rewrite. windowPerGroup() upstream of an ORF that
      starts at transcript position 1 or 2 failed with "Transcript query
      coordinates are out of bounds", which made detect_ribo_orfs() fail on
      full candidate sets.
    o Mapping validation, mixed-strand preparation, interval reduction and
      output factories now run in C++ bindings. A standalone C++11 header
      separates coordinate logic from R/Rcpp objects; input storage is borrowed.
      Full-call and storage-representation benchmarks, original baselines and
      reproduction notes live in benchmark/transcript_mapping/.

    o Paired transcript mapping borrows integer inputs and writes final output
      vectors directly. Long ordered exon searches use binary lookup; short
      and irregular groups retain bounded linear searches.
    o Mapping checks transcript boundaries, empty inputs, coordinate overflow,
      paired chromosomes and scalar references. Unmappable genomic queries
      retain the existing sentinel; invalid transcript queries report errors.
    o The to-transcript wrapper reads unlisted strand and partition offsets
      directly. Group strand/sequence accessors index Rle values before
      expansion only for large, exon-rich lists, retaining the small-list path.

Coverage performance
--------------------

    o coverageByTranscriptFST batches chromosome-aware page/exon joins and
      shares bounded reads of nearby page slices within a call. Input exon
      order, requested column order, strand reversal and independent result
      tables are preserved. Indexes/pages are reread on every call.
    o coverage_to_dt expands positive coverage runs directly, avoiding a
      one-base IRanges object per output row. Counts, gene factors, positions,
      frame columns and empty-coverage warnings are preserved.

ORFik 1.0.0
-----------------------

    o first release of ORFik - find Open Reading Frames, automatic RiboSeq
    footprint shifts, reassignment of Transcription Start Sites with the use of
    CageSeq, plethora of gene identity functions from scientific publications

Bioconductor build fixes
-----------------------

    o Genome download failures now report the underlying service error instead
      of failing while coercing an error object to a logical value.
    o The importing-data and transcript tutorials use bundled synthetic
      references for runnable examples; network download examples remain
      available as explicit, optional steps. All vignettes include session info.
    o Reference-space CIGAR widths now use cigarillo on current Bioconductor,
      with a compatibility fallback for older releases, as query-space widths do.
    o Clarified local-reference arguments, cache reuse and pseudo-leader
      interpretation, and corrected the fastp UMI example.


CHANGES IN VERSION 1.1.12
-----------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Remade many function to handle no names correctly, like tile1 will now
    work even for GRangesList without names. Documentation is more logical, and
    removed coverageByWindow, since GenomicFeatures::coverageByTranscripts now
    works correctly.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.1.12
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o The orf finding function now find the longest orf per stop codon if
      you set longestORF = TRUE in findORFS, findMapORFs and findORFsFasta

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.3.7
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o mapToGRanges is now much faster and uses much less memory. A c++
      reimplementation of pmapFromTranscripts from GenomicFeatures.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.7.0
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o The ORFik experiment syntax is ready, to simplifiy ORFik usage
    with big data.


CHANGES IN VERSION 1.7.17
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Added pmapToTranscriptsF, a much faster pmapToTranscripts.
    o All of ORFik now supports weights for representing duplicated reads.
    This will speed up all function related to NGS data a lot.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.13.7
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Massive improvement in speed of coveragePerTiling
    o Improved p-shifting analysis (also added verbose output)
    o Added possible optimization for annotation
    o Rewritten vignettes

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.23.8
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Implemented a Ribo-seq ORF detector now included
    o Added new export functions for bigwig, covRLE

STAR / fastp updates
-------------------

    o Fixed allow.introns forwarding in STAR.align.single and STAR.align.folder.
      The default TRUE now enables novel junction discovery (--alignIntronMax 0).
      Earlier affected runs silently used 1 even with TRUE. Set FALSE explicitly
      to retain that indexed-junction-only behavior; indexed splicing remains
      possible in either mode. This correction can change alignment results.
    o Added base.correction = FALSE to both entry points. TRUE enables fastp
      correction of overlapping paired reads during trimming (issue #172).
    o Pipeline logs now show each step's actual inputs, outputs and command,
      instead of repeatedly presenting the original reads as input (issue #174).
    o Fixed paired-folder multimapping option forwarding, tRNA input compression,
      and noShared memory mode across multiple libraries. Commands preserve paths
      containing spaces or shell metacharacters and stop on tool failure.
    o Empty folders, duplicate output basenames, and invalid step order now fail
      explicitly. Pairing still uses adjacent files in sorted filename order.
